## No rows overlay

When `rowData` is set to an empty array `[]`, the grid automatically displays the no-rows overlay. To control it programmatically use `activeOverlay`:

The built-in no-rows overlay can be completely disabled by setting either `noRowsOverlayComponent = false` or `components.agNoRowsOverlay = false` or `activeOverlay = false` in the grid options.

{% gridExampleRunner title="No Rows Overlay" name="no-rows-overlay"  exampleHeight=350 /%}

### Custom No Rows Overlay

The no-rows overlay can be customised via the grid properties `noRowsOverlayComponent` and `noRowsOverlayComponentParams`.
It is also possible to define `agNoRowsOverlay` in the [`components` map](./components) to provide a custom no-rows overlay component as well.

{% apiDocumentation source="grid-options/properties.json" section="overlays" names=["noRowsOverlayComponent", "noRowsOverlayComponentParams", "activeOverlayParams"] /%}

